Answer A is correct; this problem is a multiple-choice question. Solution:
Let \(x\) = time taken by Jon to complete the triathlon.
\begin{align*}40x+1.2x+50=40\\ 1.2x=40-50\\ 1.2x=-10\\ x=-\frac{10}{1.2}=-\frac{10}{12}=-\frac{5}{6}\end{align*}
\begin{align*}40\left(-\frac{5}{6}\right)+1.2\left(-\frac{5}{6}\right)+50=40\left(-\frac{5}{6}\right)+\left(-\frac{5}{6}\right)50\\ -\frac{200}{6}+\left(-\frac{5}{6}\right)50=-\frac{200}{6}+\left(-\frac{5}{6}\right)\left(50\right)\\ -\frac{200}{6}+\left(-\frac{50}{6}\right)=\left(-\frac{200}{6}\right)-\left(-\frac{50}{6}\right)\\ -\frac{200}{6}-\frac{50}{6}=-\frac{200}{6}+\frac{50}{6}\\ -\frac{250}{6}=-\frac{150}{6}\\ -\frac{250}{6}=-\frac{150}{6}\end{align*}
